{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For any man</b> etc. It is giving a reason, and this is its meaning: for any man who has a blemish in him, it does not seem proper that he should offer." "<b>Who has a blemish in him.</b> Even one born with a blemish from his mother's womb." "<b>Charem (split).<b> From the root of potsherd and breaking." "<b>Sarua (dissolved, i.e., elongated limb).</b> From the root of stretching out."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:11.094106446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}